{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021783-system-to-manage-a-settlement","id":1021783,"title":"System to manage a settlement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T20:17:21-08:00","id":1021783,"title":"System to manage a settlement","content":"I'm getting ready to run a game set in the neolithic era. My characters will become mages who look after their community and I was hoping for a system of some sort that would help me emulate a management like setup. I want them to be able to influence and direct the npc community but without just doing it, I'd like some kind of merit system maybe or treat villages as like a combination of merit points bought collectively like a totem maybe, treat it like a haven? Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T20:47:45-08:00","id":1021796,"title":"","content":"The status merit should be more than adequate to represent the individual Mage's influence over, and <i>status </i>within the settlement.<br /> Other aspects, such as the actual population, resources to use and so forth I'd keep as a narrative element. Mages in the Neolithic Era still stayed separated from their communities due to Quiescence, and spending experiences to enhance it? I think that's a bit too much like base building, and from what I've read CofD really just wants to keep that stuff abstracted, interconnecting with the character only in such a manner as it'll impact their specific plot. e.g. Safe Place, Sanctum, and social merits.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that your settlement will be a fairly big one, given that you've got an entire group of Mages looking after it.<br /> Also running that as an abstraction which the players don't have to spend experiences on to enhance means that no player will feel resentful to one another for them not investing anything in the community beyond their basic duties while instead pursuing their own mystical powers, which I would imagine many Mages would likely do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T22:00:27-08:00","id":1021829,"title":"","content":"Reading now <b>Hurt Locker</b>, I seen yesterday cool mechanics for so called Violence Groups - that in reality just could be called 'Factions mechanics'. Basically, it's subsystem for making and running small organisation, like gang, cult or any tight mortals group. As settlement of humans in <i>Sundered World</i> are <i>very rarely</i> more than 100 people, I would advise you to just make each village as each one of those groups. They get basic groups ideology ( and common Aspirations ), typical members stats or Groups Merits to be used for whole community. In my POV, it's really great stuff! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}